WEBVTT

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:04.190
Right. Hold it like that, and...

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.070
...press the knot against the pointy
part of the beigoma spinning top.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.650
"How to wrap a string around beigoma"

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.650
And then, wrap the string around it.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.490
Let's see... the way to throw it is...

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.990
Hm? The cell signal is...

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.370
Done!

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.490
Whoa!

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.910
Right? This looks like the real deal!

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.290
Let's see... Throw it! "Throw it"?

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.250
Go!

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.470
Hm?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.560
Coconuts...?

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:37.970
I'm sorry.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:41.060
I'm really sorry... Are you okay?

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.460
It probably won't spin on
rough ground like this, right?

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.990
Yeah. I wish we had something
more suitable, like a barrel--

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.570
Kokonotsu!

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.370
Let's... play!

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.830
H-Hotaru?!

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.380
Well... Um... That's...

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.670
When it comes to a stage for beigoma,
you've gotta use something like this!

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.340
Well... Um... Where'd you get it?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.550
No need to worry.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.430
What?!

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.430
I'll take off this skirt...

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.690
...and use it to make the beigoma stage!

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:55.020
This skirt has two layers. Isn't it amazing?

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.530
I-I see...

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.650
I'll say...!

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.570
Now, this will do the trick!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.990
You sure know a lot about beigoma!

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.330
Of course!

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.580
It would be no exaggeration to say that
I've mastered the art of beigoma!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.790
Beigoma, together with 
menko cards and marbles,

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:20.090
make up the Three Sacred
Treasures of dagashi toys.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.640
Beigoma in particular 
has seen the development

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.930
of many unique techniques
throughout its long history of battles.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.020
Now, just watch.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.140
Hotaru's Gale Throw!

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.150
Coconuts!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.030
Kokonotsu?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.660
Pull it... like this!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.410
Pull and throw!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.580
They're spinning!

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.960
That's right. It's important to
pull back when you throw it.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.210
It's the theory of "What's the harm?"
seen in samurai dramas.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.340
"What's the harm?"

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.210
"Oh no!"

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.760
S-Say what?

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.050
How foolish!

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.300
When playing beigoma, throwing yours last...

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.640
...gives you an overwhelming advantage!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.070
I-I'm sure you'll do better next time.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.900
The essence of beigoma extends
far beyond simple technique.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.370
Warriors from olden times put their
heart and souls into their beigoma

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.160
and continuously strived to
improve its strength and beauty.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.080
And then, finally, as the result
of overcoming many hardships,

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.710
the strongest beigoma was born!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:39.670
"Ho"

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.750
Here comes... Hotaru Special!

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:40.800
Whoa!

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.380
The real battle begins now.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.680
The one whose beigoma keeps
spinning until the end wins!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:51.130
And, the loser will do anything
the winner asks them to do.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.100
How does that sound?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.440
A real battle, huh? Count me in!

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.110
Right. I've got only one wish.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.030
I want you to take over Shikada Dagashi.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.450
Ah!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.160
So this is where you guys were!
What're you doing?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.580
Master Saya!

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.380
So this will do? This is kinda cute!

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.380
Everyone, are you ready?!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.680
Go! Hotaru Special!

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.060
Here we... go!

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.140
All right!

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.140
It's spinning! It's spinning!

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.490
Go!

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.940
There! Go!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.400
All right!

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.900
Hotaru, you're really good.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.900
So is Saya.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.410
Come on!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.200
Go!

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.160
I'd expect no less from
Master Saya, the game genius.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.000
But genius or not, my strongest
beigoma is... unbeatable!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.340
"Ho"

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.000
All right!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.560
Hotaru Special!

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.310
It went flying big time, so...

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.810
It may not be in this area.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.300
I thought it came flying over here.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:24.610
Hotaru! Any luck over... there?!

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:30.110
Hmm... I can't find it. How about you?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.790
No...

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.580
Coconuts.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.580
S-Saya!

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.880
N-No, it's not like that.
You've got it all wrong!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.840
"Ho"

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.140
Welcome-- Hm?

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:58.980
She's here.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.440
She's here again.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.070
That weird kid came again.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.650
This shop is as disorganized as ever.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:13.950
Customers can't find anything like this.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.870
In addition, most of the
shelves are positioned too high.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.710
Kids will have a hard time reaching them.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.290
I wonder if you're even 
aware that's a problem.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:29.090
That kid who won't shut up about how
to run a dagashi shop is here again.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:32.170
That being said, the fact that 
you don't try to make the shop

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:34.380
look unnaturally clean and tidy,

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:37.310
does give this place a genuine charm.
I'll give you props for that.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.060
Is it possible... that you've been
doing this on purpose?

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.440
I see. You're pretty shrewd.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.940
Well then, do you know 
when dagashi were born?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.820
It is said that the first dagashi was created

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.950
using millet and starch
syrup during the Edo Era.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.290
Err... Around that time, um...

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.750
It was called "Ichi-mon snack"...

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.960
since it was a snack for commoners that
could be purchased only for one mon.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.630
That's right!

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.840
Let's see... Well then...

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.970
"200 yen"

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.720
Well then, how about this beigoma here?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.600
It's said that it started when people played
using bai-gai seashells during the Heian era.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.850
It was first called "baigoma," and then
at some point it became "beigoma."

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.770
Wow, that's amazing!

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.150
I hope you keep up the good work!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:35.160
After all, this is the 
only dagashi shop in town!

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.450
Try smiling a bit.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:43.660
Your face is scary.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:48.380
With that face, even if customers come,
they'll just run away as fast as they can.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.420
Now, like this.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.390
See?

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.980
Try it. Now.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.680
"Rumble, rumble, rumble..."

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:01.830
A devil...

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.190
I don't think you'll get customers like that.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.400
Come to think of it, I've been to
this shop several times now,

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:12.860
but I rarely see... other customers.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.450
Perhaps kids these days...

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.200
...just don't have an 
interest in dagashi anymore.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.830
Oops... Sorry.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.340
"General Goods and Dagashi / Morimoto Store"

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.750
I shouldn't have said that to a customer.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.830
I will come again tomorrow...
and the day after, too.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.100
I'll keep coming day after day...

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.520
...so long as the place has dagashi!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.310
"Hokkaido Dice Caramel"

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.310
I'll take these.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:48.990
Keep the change.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.990
"Keep the change"?

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.530
This is the exact amount.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:07.160
"Land for Sale"

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.420
"General Goods and Dagashi / Morimoto Store"

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.630
"Kokonotsu"
"Calling"

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.630
Yes? Hello, Hotaru.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.300
What's up?

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.640
Sorry, I'm not calling
for any particular reason.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:25.520
Um...

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.560
Kokonotsu.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.770
You know... I love Shikada Dagashi.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:34.230
What...? What?! Wh-What 
is it all of a sudden?

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:37.990
"Beigoma, Reminiscence, and..."

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:37.320
A-Ah... D-Dagashi...! 
Oh, the shop...! Yeah...

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time: Homerun Bar, 
Fireworks Festival, and..."

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.410
Next time: "Homerun Bar,
Fireworks Festival, and..."

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.950
You hold onto this.
